---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Authors" description="Who writes the notes. Open to the house.">
  <h1>Authors</h1>

  <p>
    Notes live in git. You write a markdown file, you put your handle in the
    frontmatter, you push (or open a PR). That is the CMS. No CMS.
  </p>

  <p>
    Path: <code>sites/tharavad/src/content/blog/</code>. Fields:
    <code>title</code>, <code>date</code>, <code>summary</code>,
    <code>author</code>. Plain text supremacy. If the site and the repo
    disagree, trust the repo.
  </p>

  <p>
    Looking for maintainers and resident seats? That moved to
    <a href="/house/">The house</a> — crew + roster, not a LinkedIn carousel.
    Ship history: <a href="/log/">Ship log</a>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Got a seat? Land a note under your handle. We are not a sole-author brand
    kit. Members write. Git keeps score.
  </p>
</Base>
